(DocChat AI Vector Storage & Persistence - Page 3) '
(Once vector embeddings are generated, chunks and their metadata are committed to a persistent ChromaDB collection via ChromaVectorStore. ChromaDB persists vector indexes to the local filesystem using HNSW hierarchical navigable small-world graphs configured with cosine similarity distance metrics.) '
(The ChromaVectorStore exposes a clean public interface featuring add_chunks\(\) for upserting vectorized content, list_documents\(\) for inventorying indexed documents with aggregated chunk counts, and delete_document\(doc_id\) for atomic deletion of all vector chunks associated with an unindexed document.) '
(This ingestion architecture guarantees high retrieval accuracy, sub-50ms vector query latencies, and deterministic isolation between distinct documents.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
